A||N||18||fropuff||Fog lamps anyone?||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||08-21-2000||12:19 AM||||Hey, I'm thinking about putting some fog lamps in my front fascia next to the plate bracket but slightly "in".  I am looking for any ideas of what light I should use.  I like the round style like DXR_DAD's and OREIF's.  I was thinking of using some rectangular ones, ones that are long and skinny.  Just got to make sure not to drop one and have it shatter.  I'm still mad about that one.  Anyway, any of you with some fog lamps that can give me some info?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||08-21-2000||01:00 AM||||Just a thought fropuff, but I've been thinking about the same thing. What came to mind is using something like the driving lights off of a late model cavalier, they are angled on the side and might mold nicely into the contours of the GT's air sucker.. Keep us appraised of what you decide. Oh and we are still waiting for the pics of your paint job.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||08-21-2000||01:38 AM|||| <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=522257&a=3823750&p=21230303" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=522257&a=3823750&p=21230303</A>  this is what i have, they are rectangle.<p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 08-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-21-2000||01:42 AM||||fropuff--Do you want fog lights or driving lights??  Huge difference in the light pattern.  The fog lights throw a very short but wide pattern whereas the driving lights throw a narrow but skinny pattern.  Personally, I think fog lights are just about worthless.  If it's that damn foggy, I'll just stay home.  On the other hand, I have no problem driving at night.<P>Unless you live somewhere that is very prone to fog (and I see that you don't), I would suggest driving lights instead.  And remember, you usually get what you pay for.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Uaana||08-21-2000||01:55 AM||||OMG!! I'm gonna disagree with Monkeyman..<BR>For those who live by Superior (Duluth), fog is a big problem. And for those of us in the snow belt, A heavy snow is worse than fog. I once went 40mi with only the fogs on cause it was better than driving with the headlights on. <BR>So the question returns to Fogs or Driving lights fropuff?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-21-2000||02:06 AM||||Oops!  I misread where he was from.  I thought it said, "Saginaw, <B>MI</B>", not <B>MN</B>.  Sorry.  Since you live in the snow belt (been there, done that, many times) you just might consider fog lights.  Driving lights in snow=blindness.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||08-21-2000||05:16 AM||||the gt's air sucker.. hehe.  somebody's gotta start collecting all these technical Fiero terms and make a little "PFF guide to Fiero parts"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000007||Philphine||08-21-2000||07:53 AM||||i've had a few sets of combo fog/driving lights. if you can find a style that fits where you want it's just a little extra wiring and you have both. at this time on my '87 (formula front end) i have about 2"X6" combo lights. never got around to wireing them up and will probaly take them off since i should be changing to a gt facia soon.<P>around the time i got my indy scoop i came across a pair of tiny driving lights that i thought i'd put in/on it. got it half worked out but i thought i had heard that there are laws about how high lights can be mounted. it might still be lower than a lifted 4wd though. if nothing else it would look different than a regular indy scoop. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||08-21-2000||09:14 AM||||Thanks for all the replies.  I'm gonna have to go with the fog lamps.  It does get foggy here pretty often.  I'm not going to drive my car in the snow, so that doesn't really matter.  All I'm actually looking for is the look.  Yes, they can serve a little bit of a purpose, but I'm going for the look.  I like the ones that Al have; haven't seen the Cavailer ones.  I'll have to look into those.  Al, how do the lights fit?  Do they take up a lot of space?  Thanks a lot.<P>Oh, I will be posting pics of my GT sometime.  Got it buffed yesterday; doesn't look like a show car, but I don't want a show car!  If I did, I would have paid the $1500.  I also need to repair my lens for my back-up lights.  Yes, I dropped one while mounting it.  That sucked!  I gotta look for a glue that won't show the cracks as bad and that will cover in the chip gaps.  Then, I'm putting the molding on today.  Should be pretty soon.  I'm just glad it got done before school starts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  ||||reg||1
